        "id": 188602,
        "name": "Dandolo",
        "username": "Dandolo",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dandolo/{size}/1845_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-02-01T13:12:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You can watch how LewdDolphin played it by going here <a href=\"https://youtu.be/QjT7j7xyJLsAs\">https://youtu.be/QjT7j7xyJLsAs</a> to my game I feel the big keys was playing Grease Gun right before the Prison Riot and opening up Ra’s first turn with Imbued Fire.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Those were the key for me as well, though for me Grease Gun was played after Prison Riot to buy me some time to deal with all the targets. The other key move I made was moving 3 non-target environment cards from the environment trash to the bottom of an empty environment deck using Excavation to buy a few rounds of peace.</p>",
