      {
        "id": 188605,
        "name": "LewdDolphin21",
        "username": "LewdDolphin21",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lewddolphin21/{size}/1893_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-02-01T14:31:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"robb8888\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> robb8888:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>LewdDolphin21 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I played Subzero Atmosphere smartly, making sure not to destroy it during Akash'bhuta's play phase, and actually spared the team a lot of damage from Living Rockslides (actually, no Rockslide ever dealt damage, which was cool).\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;When/how did you ever see Subzero Atmosphere? &nbsp;I'm in the middle of my first (and looking to be unsuccessful) try -- I'm on at least Round 5 or so (the first Prison Riot/Eruption has come), and there's no Subzero Atmosphere in sight. &nbsp;I played Sub-Zero's \"grab your favorite module from the deck then draw a card\" card -- maybe that made my shuffle different than yours?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I got it on my third turn by playing my third Onboard Module Installation. What you get definitely changes based on which Modules you select, since the differing deck contents would affect the deck shuffle.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:14:36.785Z",
