        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/deddragon/{size}/2335_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-02-05T15:44:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Got a Near Mint after a few critical early mistakes in the first game.</p>\n<p>Absolute Zero was a big damage dealer in my winning game, couldn’t have done it without him. I got Thermal Shockwave out, which combined with Isothermic Transducer and Imbued Fire was doing 2 damage 4 times each round with only 1 damage to himself.<br>\nKNYFE didn’t have her own buffs, so she took advantage of the fire as well. Do I want to hit AZ a second time with Incidental Contact? Yes, yes I do.<br>\nLike has been said, Excavation was really handy to help keep Akash from flipping and giving a little respite from limbs. And of course Ra bounced a little Inferno damage off Zero when he ran out of targets.<br>\nTempest spent a few turns unable to do damage, but still contributed with a Ball Lightning and some Correspondence on those rounds. Did some damage on other rounds with a burning Hurricane.<br>\nNot Fixer’s best match but he did 2-5 damage most rounds.<br>\nI enjoyed arranging for Guards to hit limbs when they were out. I even let Char get the killing blow on Akash.<br>\nEveryone was up at the end, though Tempest was at 1 and Absolute Zero was at 2.</p>",
